From f6c4a554e4faecdf8fdb74b8e21ee55c27291f9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:03:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/28] tools: add pullify.py, a rewriter that turns upstream
 workflows into pull-model ones

The generator workflows are ~5,000 lines of YAML that upstream changes
often. Instead of hand-rebasing edits to them on every sync, this script
applies the pull-model changes mechanically and idempotently, keeping
upstream's formatting and comments:

- workflow_dispatch inputs: zip_url -> cfg, build_uuid, proto. The
  run-name carries the build uuid, and the setup job passes build_uuid.
- Top-level permissions: contents: read, actions: write.
- Steps that POST to /cleanzip, set STATUS_URL (/updategh) or upload to
  an API server's /api/save_custom_client are removed. Job-level env:
  keys left empty are dropped.
- Steps that POST builds to <GENURL>/save_custom_client become
  actions/upload-artifact steps named rdgen-<build_uuid>-<job>-<index>,
  with retention-days: 1, compression-level: 0 and
  if-no-files-found: error. Paths are parsed from the curl -F file=@...
  arguments.
- /get_png downloads (pwsh Invoke-WebRequest, wget, and macOS's
  multi-line curl||wget) become copies from $RUNNER_TEMP/rdgen-assets.
- Patch downloads from raw.githubusercontent.com/bryangerlach/rdgen
  master become copies from $RUNNER_TEMP/rdgen-patches (this commit's
  .github/patches, staged by decrypt-secrets). The printer-adapter
  checkout of bryangerlach/rdgen@master becomes ${{ github.repository }}
  at ${{ github.sha }}. Builds therefore run only code from the
  user's own repository at the dispatched commit.
- Every remote action is pinned to a full commit SHA (resolved with git
  ls-remote on 2026-09-30). @master/@main of the artifact actions map to
  their latest release (download v8.0.1, upload v7.0.1).
  github-script@v6 (node16) maps to v7. Upstream's trailing comments are
  kept.
- Existing upload-artifact steps without retention-days get 1 day. This
  covers the Linux .deb upload, which carries custom_.txt with the preset
  password and had no retention (90 days by default).
- Workflows the pull model does not use are deleted, because a token with
  Actions: write can start any workflow_dispatch workflow:
  sh-generator-windows.yml (the SH_SECRET variant), build-web.yml,
  clear-cache.yml (purges all caches), vcpkg.yml, and docker-build.yml
  (runs on every push and pushes a Docker image). An unknown new
  workflow with its own trigger fails the check.

Post-conditions are checked on every run: no callback URLs, no upstream
master fetches, every action pinned, and an rdgen artifact upload in each
generator. An unknown action or a new callback step makes it exit 2, so
an automated upstream sync stops instead of pushing a half-converted
tree. --check only reports (exit 1 when a rewrite is pending).

